Backend-only FastAPI service using uv, SQLite and systemd.
{% if enable_jobs %}
Includes Redis-backed Taskiq workers and a separate interval scheduler.
{% endif %}

## Development

```bash
task setup
cp .env.example .env
uv run {{ cli_command }} init-db
uv run {{ cli_command }} serve
```

Run commands from the project root. Python is selected from `.python-version`.
All commands and systemd services load the same `.env` automatically. Exported
environment variables override the file. Settings are loaded once per process;
restart services after changing configuration.

{% if enable_jobs %}
Install Redis (Ubuntu: `sudo apt install redis-server`) and start it before running the API.
In separate terminals:

```bash
uv run {{ cli_command }} worker
uv run {{ cli_command }} scheduler
uv run {{ cli_command }} enqueue "hello"
```

The scheduler sleeps for the configured interval between dispatches. Submissions
do not overlap. Missed executions during downtime are not replayed. Taskiq uses a per-project Redis stream and retains results for 24 hours.
Task delivery can be repeated after worker failure; design side effects to be idempotent.
{% endif %}

## API

- `GET /health/live`: process liveness.
- `GET /health` or `GET /health/ready`: SQLite{% if enable_jobs %} and Redis{% endif %} readiness, returning 503 on dependency failure.
- `GET /messages/count`: sample persisted message count.
{% if enable_jobs %}
- `POST /jobs`: submit `{"message":"hello"}`, returning a job ID and HTTP 202.
{% endif %}
- `GET /docs`: interactive OpenAPI documentation.

Keep the default loopback binding unless authentication and network exposure
are explicitly configured.

{% if enable_mcp %}
## MCP for AI agents

The official MCP Python SDK serves Streamable HTTP on the existing API process.
Connect your MCP client to `http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp/` (adjust the port if configured).
The included `get_message_count` tool reads the same SQLite database as the HTTP API.
Add explicitly scoped tools in `mcp_server.py`; do not expose arbitrary shell commands,
filesystem access or all HTTP routes automatically. DNS rebinding protection stays enabled.
The endpoint is unauthenticated and intended for loopback use only. Configure authentication,
TLS and explicit host/origin allowlists before remote exposure.

Example client configuration (client-specific keys may vary):

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "{{ project_slug }}": {
      "url": "http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp/"
    }
  }
}
```

{% endif %}
## Ubuntu deployment

After running `uv sync` and configuring `.env`, execute:

```bash
sudo bash deploy/install.sh
sudo systemctl status {{ project_slug }}-api.service
sudo journalctl -fu {{ project_slug }}-api.service
```

The installer enables the API{% if enable_jobs %}, worker and scheduler{% endif %} at boot under a non-root account.
To update, run `uv sync --frozen --no-dev` as the service user and restart the installed units.
Commit the generated `uv.lock` to your repository.

## Tests

```bash
task check
task benchmark
task resources
```

Pull-request CI delegates quality and distribution checks to centralized reusable workflows.

`task setup` installs the staged-file Ruff hooks when run in a Git repository root.
Run `task fix` to format the whole project. Benchmarks produce `.benchmarks/latest.json`.
The resources command reports machine memory and the CLI process RSS, not server RSS.
